IO-23: report a unit hydrograph group that has no rain gage

A [HYDROGRAPHS] group's rain gage is set only by its "Name Gage" line, and
UnitHyd[] is calloc'ed, so a group without that line silently used gage
index 0: a gage that nothing else uses keeps its first rainfall value for
the whole run, and with no gages in the project initGageData() reads past
the end of Gage[]. rdii_initUnitHyd() now sets the gage to -1 and
validateRdii() reports the new ERROR 152 for a group without one.

Apply from the root of a Stormwater-Management-Model checkout at cb3e192b:
    git apply IO-23_swmm530.patch

diff --git a/src/legacy/engine/error.h b/src/legacy/engine/error.h
index 2bcea19..a4850f4 100644
--- a/src/legacy/engine/error.h
+++ b/src/legacy/engine/error.h
@@ -102,6 +102,8 @@ enum ErrorType {
 // ... RDII Errors
       /*! \brief RDII unit hydrograph time error */
       ERR_UNITHYD_TIMES        = 151,
+      /*! \brief RDII unit hydrograph has no rain gage */
+      ERR_UNITHYD_GAGE         = 152,
       /*! \brief RDII unit hydrograph ratios error */
       ERR_UNITHYD_RATIOS       = 153,
       /*! \brief RDII area error */
